🧪 How Gaia Tests Must Be Executed

✅ Gaia tests must be executed with the project running locally

🖥️ Local execution (your machine)

🤖 Remote execution via Jenkins, but still running a dedicated environment

🎯 Goal:

🧱 A separate environment that does not interfere with other teams

🗄️ A dedicated database for Gaia validation

🌙 Best Time to Run

✅ The project can be run at any time

🌙 Prefer night time / off-hours for performance

🟢 Machines are not turned off, so overnight execution is allowed

🚀 After Every Release (Mandatory Checklist)

✅ Update the local project to the new release version

✅ Run a git pull to get the latest changes

✅ Perform a cache clean (to avoid stale artifacts)

