🛠️ Local Machine Setup
✅ Step 1: Clone the Projects (Web + Backend)

📥 Clone both repositories:

🌐 Web (Front)

🧱 Backend (Back)

✅ Step 2: Stay on the Master Branch

📌 Ensure you are on master:

git checkout master
git pull
✅ Step 3: Install the ZIP with node_modules

📦 Use the provided ZIP containing all node_modules

🎯 Purpose:

🚀 Faster setup

✅ Standardized dependencies across the team

🌐 Frontend Setup (Front)
✅ Step 1: Place .npmrc in the User Root (C:)

📌 Copy .npmrc to:

C:\Users\<YOUR_USER>\.npmrc

✅ Step 2: Install Dependencies

📂 Open a terminal inside the frontend project folder:

npm i
✅ Step 3: Update Credentials in .npmrc

🔐 Open .npmrc and replace:

User and Password with your own

🧩 Also change the text below the second user/password to:

✍️ <PLACE_PHRASE_HERE>

🔒 Tip: Treat .npmrc as sensitive and avoid committing it to git.

✅ Step 4: Start the Frontend
npm start
🧱 Backend Setup (Back)
